{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Complex","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Trigonometric","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.c_rule_is_vacuous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.c_rule_is_vacuous","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/N1FactorUniqueness.lean#L156-L164","doc":"**CONTROL — the C limit is not an accident of `δ = 0` arithmetic.**\n\nUnder convention C the bar action is `a ↦ -a` and `cos` is even, so the\nbar-midpoint rule returns its input unchanged: the rule is *vacuous* in C.  That\nis why C could carry a bare cosine, and the reason its unavailability under D is\nstructural rather than a gap in the search. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.uncentred_fails_of_pos_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.uncentred_fails_of_pos_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/N1FactorUniqueness.lean#L142-L154","doc":"The physically relevant form: for a defect strictly between `0` and `2π` —\nwhich the D-frame `δ = h²/2` is, being small and positive — the un-recentred\ncosine is not bar-invariant.  Needs only `0 < π`, no numeric bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.uncentred_fails","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.uncentred_fails","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/N1FactorUniqueness.lean#L130-L140","doc":"**CONTROL — the forcing has teeth.**\n\nIf bar-invariance held for every `c`, everything above would be vacuous.  It\ndoes not: the *un-recentred* cosine (`c = 0`, the convention-C form) is\nbar-invariant only in the degenerate case `δ = 2kπ`.  Stated for arbitrary `δ`\nrather than at one sample point, and proved from `phase_forced` itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.c_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.c_limit","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/N1FactorUniqueness.lean#L121-L128","doc":"**The convention-C limit.**  At `δ = 0` the factor is a bare cosine, which\nis condition (iii); and there the bar action is `a ↦ -a`, under which `cos` is\nalready invariant.  This is why C could use a bare cosine and D cannot — the\nbar-midpoint rule is *vacuous* in C, not satisfied by accident. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.barMidpoint_barInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.barMidpoint_barInvariant","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/N1FactorUniqueness.lean#L116-L119","doc":"The arc's chosen factor `M(a) = cos(a - δ/2)·cos(δ/2)` is bar-invariant —\nthe entry-2 bar-midpoint rule's output, in the forced phase. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.phase_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.phase_forced","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/N1FactorUniqueness.lean#L92-L114","doc":"**The phase re-centring is FORCED**, modulo `π`.\n\nBar-invariance for a nonzero `K` holds **iff** `c = δ/2 - kπ` for some integer\n`k`.  The arc's continuity argument (`c(0) = 0`, `c` continuous) selects\n`k = 0`, giving `c = δ/2`; that selection is outside this statement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.const_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.const_free","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/N1FactorUniqueness.lean#L83-L90","doc":"**The constant is FREE.**  For *every* `K`, re-centring by `δ/2` gives a\nbar-invariant factor.  So conditions (i)–(iii) leave `K` unconstrained — a\nproved negative, not an unfound constraint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.barMidpoint_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.barMidpoint_eq","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/N1FactorUniqueness.lean#L69-L81","doc":"**The bar-midpoint identity — the step `sympy.simplify` would not do.**\n\n`(cos a + cos(δ - a))/2 = cos(a - δ/2) · cos(δ/2)`, exactly, for all real `a`\nand `δ`.  Entry 10 verified this at 60 dps after the CAS returned a non-zero\nresidual; it is an identity, and this is the proof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.BarInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.BarInvariant","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/N1FactorUniqueness.lean#L66-L67","doc":"Bar-invariance of a candidate, as a proposition in `a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.candidate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.candidate","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/N1FactorUniqueness.lean#L62-L64","doc":"The candidate `N = 1` factor in the log-separable form the arc requires:\na cosine re-centred by `c`, times a phase-independent constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.barPhase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.N1FactorUniqueness.barPhase","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/N1FactorUniqueness.lean#L58-L60","doc":"The bar action on the D-frame phase: `a ↦ δ - a`, a reflection about `δ/2`.\nUnder convention C, `δ = 0` and this is the familiar `a ↦ -a`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}